{
    "id": "meals_dialer",
    "title": "The Convoso Dialer",
    "est_minutes": 18,
    "summary": "Logging in, your status, the agent screen, the transfer flow and dispositioning for the Meals campaign.",
    "badge": {
        "id": "badge_meals_dialer",
        "name": "Dialer Ready",
        "icon": "☎️"
    },
    "lessons": [
        {
            "id": "m8_1",
            "title": "Logging in",
            "est_minutes": 4,
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "type": "callout",
                    "tone": "warning",
                    "title": "Use Google Chrome",
                    "html": "<p>Other browsers cause audio problems that look like dialer faults and waste your shift.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "html": "<p>Sign in with your email and password. In the pop-up choose the <strong>Meals</strong> campaign and set your status to <strong>Available</strong> or <strong>Break</strong>, then Login.</p><p>Check the campaign every time — the wrong one means the wrong leads and the wrong script.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "html": "<p>You are Available or Break at all times, nothing else. Allow the browser's audio permission when it asks, or calls connect to silence.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "html": "<p>Logging out: set status to <strong>Break</strong> first (top right), then Logout at the bottom.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "check",
                    "question": "Before logging out you should…",
                    "choices": [
                        "Switch campaign",
                        "Set status to Break, then Logout",
                        "Disposition and walk away",
                        "Just close the tab"
                    ],
                    "answer_index": 1,
                    "explanation": "Break first, then Logout."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "m8_2",
            "title": "The agent screen",
            "est_minutes": 4,
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "html": "<p><strong>Top left</strong> — call status, and on a live call the consumer's name and a running timer.</p><p><strong>Top right</strong> — the blue <strong>Transfer</strong> button brings the conference tab back; the red <strong>Wrap Up</strong> button ends a call.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "html": "<p><strong>Left sidebar</strong> — Availability (change it before a call lands, you can't while you're on one) and the dispositions.</p><p><strong>Tabs</strong> — Script holds your script and the conference button; Contact holds the consumer's details including their borough and ZIP.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "callout",
                    "tone": "warning",
                    "title": "Dispositioning ends the call",
                    "html": "<p>Make sure you're finished before you click, and code what actually happened.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "check",
                    "question": "Where's the conference transfer button?",
                    "choices": [
                        "Dial pad",
                        "Left sidebar",
                        "Contact tab",
                        "Script tab"
                    ],
                    "answer_index": 3,
                    "explanation": "On the Script tab."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "m8_3",
            "title": "The transfer",
            "est_minutes": 5,
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "html": "<p>Once all four verifications are done and the consumer has said okay:</p><ol><li>Click the conference transfer button on the Script tab</li><li>Stay on the line while it rings</li><li>When the screener answers, do the warm handoff — name, borough, ZIP</li><li>Wait until they're talking to each other</li><li>Leave the conference, then disposition</li></ol>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "callout",
                    "tone": "tip",
                    "title": "The Contact tab has the borough and ZIP",
                    "html": "<p>If they've gone out of your head mid-transfer, they're one click away. Guessing the borough in a handoff is how a Queens consumer ends up with a Bronx screener.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "html": "<p>If the consumer hangs up during the transfer, clear the screener's line first, then code it Hung-Up Transfer.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "check",
                    "question": "The consumer hangs up while the screener's line is ringing.",
                    "choices": [
                        "Clear the screener's line, then code Hung-Up Transfer",
                        "Try the transfer again",
                        "Leave both lines open",
                        "Disposition as Not Interested"
                    ],
                    "answer_index": 0,
                    "explanation": "Clear the line, then code it correctly."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "m8_4",
            "title": "Coding and miscodes",
            "est_minutes": 5,
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "html": "<p>Disposition every call, and code what happened. On this campaign the codes feed both pay and QA, so a miscode isn't an admin slip — it changes the numbers.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "callout",
                    "tone": "warning",
                    "title": "DQ is not a failure",
                    "html": "<p>There's a temptation to code a DQ as something softer, or to transfer it and let the screener deal with it. Both are worse than the DQ. Catching a disqualified consumer is a correct outcome and it's counted as one.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "html": "<p>If you miscode by accident, report it simply: the number, then the correction. Keep it short and clear for QA.</p>"
                },
                {
                    "type": "check",
                    "question": "You realise you coded a DQ as Not Interested. What do you do?",
                    "choices": [
                        "Leave it",
                        "Report the number and the correction to QA",
                        "Change it quietly next time",
                        "Call the consumer back"
                    ],
                    "answer_index": 1,
                    "explanation": "Report it — short and clear."
                }
            ]
        }
    ],
